    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 70,
      "text": "5) I have heard the arguments of Ld. APP for State and Ld. Counsel for accused.",
      "rhetorical_role": "NONE",
      "start": 3017,
      "end": 3096,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": false
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 71,
      "text": "I have also perused the record carefully.",
      "rhetorical_role": "NONE",
      "start": 3097,
      "end": 3138,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": false
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 72,
      "text": "6) It is fundamental principle of criminal jurisprudence that an accused is presumed to be innocent and therefore, the burden lies on the prosecution to prove the guilt of the accused beyond reasonable doubt.",
      "rhetorical_role": "NONE",
      "start": 3139,
      "end": 3348,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": false
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 73,
      "text": "The general burden of establishing the guilt of accused is always on the prosecution and it never shifts.",
      "rhetorical_role": "ANALYSIS",
      "start": 3349,
      "end": 3454,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.6709094643592834
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 74,
      "text": "7) In the present case, complainant Sh. Anil Bansal and witnesses Ms. Taripa D. and Savita Bahal were the only material witnesses for the prosecution out of which the complainant had expired and other two witnesses are not traceable.",
      "rhetorical_role": "NONE",
      "start": 3455,
      "end": 3689,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "Anil Bansal",
          "label": "WITNESS",
          "start": 3496,
          "end": 3507
        },
        {
          "text": "Taripa D.",
          "label": "WITNESS",
          "start": 3526,
          "end": 3535
        },
        {
          "text": "Savita Bahal",
          "label": "WITNESS",
          "start": 3540,
          "end": 3552
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": false
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 75,
      "text": "Undoubtedly, the testimony of complainant/eye- witness is material one in such cases and their non-availability become fatal to the prosecution case as they are the material witnesses, who could have proved their complaint, deposed regarding the alleged incident, identify the accused in the Court.",
      "rhetorical_role": "RATIO",
      "start": 3690,
      "end": 3988,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.6624917984008789
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 76,
      "text": "Other witnesses cited by the prosecution are police officials or Nodal officers who at the most could have deposed regarding the police proceedings,\nwhich is not sufficient to bring home the guilt of the accused in the present case.",
      "rhetorical_role": "RATIO",
      "start": 3989,
      "end": 4221,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "Nodal",
          "label": "GPE",
          "start": 4054,
          "end": 4059
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.49576714634895325
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 77,
      "text": "None of them are the eyewitness of the incident in question.",
      "rhetorical_role": "RATIO",
      "start": 4222,
      "end": 4282,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": false,
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.44122979044914246
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 78,
      "text": "In these circumstances, accused is entitled to every benefit of doubt accruing in his favour.",
      "rhetorical_role": "NONE",
      "start": 4283,
      "end": 4376,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": false
    },
    {
